{"type":"record","name":"IbkrPreOpenBaselineRevocation","namespace":"app.options.ibkr.gex","doc":"A DURABLE revocation of a baseline epoch, under the reserved key __baseline-revocation|<tradeDate>|<epoch>. A distinct namespace from the output-generation counter: the two are independent and must never alias. It makes a dropped epoch non-restorable, so a restart can never treat it as active again. Published to options.ibkr.gex.status by databento-gex-service's pre-open IBKR GEX publisher (IbkrPreOpenService). That topic carried hand-built JSON strings until the 2026-10-18 cutover, which ROLLED IT FORWARD under its own name - the topic was wiped and recreated carrying Avro, not renamed to a versioned sibling: topics in this estate are rolled forward under their own name and versioned topic names are being removed. This record reproduces that JSON FIELD FOR FIELD AND NAME FOR NAME. That is a hard requirement, not tidiness: the feed gateway converts these records to JSON for the browser with AvroJson, which emits exactly the published record's own fields, and option-chain.js reads them BY NAME. Renaming or retyping a field here changes what the browser receives. The registry subject is this record's FULL NAME, under RecordNameStrategy. That is deliberate and not the Confluent default, and here it is load-bearing rather than merely conventional: this ONE topic carries nine distinct value shapes, and a topic-name subject could not hold nine schemas. It also keeps one subject across environments, where TopicNameStrategy would mint a different subject per environment because the topic name carries the environment's TOPIC_PREFIX.","fields":[{"name":"reason","type":"string","doc":"Why the epoch was revoked, for example BASELINE_INCOMPATIBLE_WITH_REARMED_MANIFEST or RESTORED_IDENTITY_RETIRED_ON_REARM."},{"name":"atMs","type":"long","doc":"When the revocation was committed, in epoch milliseconds. The browser anchors its server clock from the first present of serverTimeMs, eventTimeMs, atMs, effectiveTimeMs, so this field's NAME is part of the contract."}]}